invariant: INV-16
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_host
reason: ch_srv_record_init stops writing the session's ch_cfg.cpu into its record
  directions, so each record it seals or opens runs under 0, which names
  no fast path: Poly1305 on the decomposition, whatever the value states.
  The key exchange and the signature still follow the multiply bit, so
  only a count of the record's copy notices: test/tcp_nonblocking_loop_widemul.h
  requires an end whose ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY to
  call no file under its own names.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    tlsi_record_cpu(&r->t);
#endif
--- new
